Subject: [PATCH] The 13-town comparison: what an expert agent would sell about
 each town, and a live homes strip for each

The approved redesign, every word kept, plus 2 to 3 sentences per town from 33 facts an independent verifier checked against official sources (city, county, state and operators' own pages): the parks, boat landings, festivals, libraries and services that make each town itself. A homes strip per town (idx-lib/places.js town-*, a short radius around each town). Those 13 places are marked index:false: their /homes/near/ pages are noindex and left out of the homes sitemap, so they never compete with the town guides.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
