 ## 4. Little River: old gardens on the waterway, and boat slips
 Little River has a county park on the Intracoastal Waterway: Vereen Memorial Historical Gardens, more than 115 acres of forest and marsh with trails and boardwalks. A piece of the original Kings Highway, the colonial road between Boston and Charleston, is still at the front of the park.
+Each October, Little River ShrimpFest fills the old waterfront with more than 200 vendors and two music stages; 2026 was its 20th year. Glen Dornoch Waterway Golf Links, in Little River, is set among live oaks, with views over the marsh and the Intracoastal Waterway. The county's North Strand Recreation Center, on SC 57 in Little River, has a full-size gym, an indoor walking track, a climbing wall and fitness classes.
 U.S. government aerial photo, 2023
 Two of Little River's marinas share one basin off the Intracoastal Waterway, with slips sold with their own deed.
 
 Boats are the other draw. About 2 in 3 of the county's boat slips sold with their own deed and tax bill are here.
 Little River is not a town, so the county makes the rules. There is no city tax, and trash goes to a private hauler or a county drop-off center.
 Half the houses here sold for more than $380,000, and half for less. Nearly every sale was a resale, not a new house.
